          "dense_rank": 1,
          "lexical_score": 6.280648,
          "lexical_rank": 1,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Vaccinations\n## COVID-19 vaccine\n\nWe offer the updated COVID-19 vaccine for the current season made by Pfizer-BioNTech (Comirnaty). We do not stock the Moderna (Spikevax) or Novavax vaccines.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 32,
          "chunk_index": 5,
          "similarity_score": 0.44467527,
          "dense_rank": 2,
          "lexical_score": null,
          "lexical_rank": null,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Vaccinations\n## After your vaccination\n\nPlease stay in the waiting area for 15 minutes after any vaccination, so staff can help if you feel faint or have an allergic reaction. A sore arm for a day or two is common. Bring your vaccination record to the appointment so the new dose can be added to it.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 32,
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "similarity_score": 0.4249558,
          "dense_rank": 3,
          "lexical_score": null,
          "lexical_rank": null,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Vaccinations\n## Tetanus, diphtheria and whooping cough (Tdap)\n\nAdults need a tetanus booster every 10 years. We use Boostrix, which also protects against diphtheria and whooping cough (pertussis).",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 32,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.4069636,
          "dense_rank": 4,
          "lexical_score": null,
          "lexical_rank": null,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Vaccinations\n## Seasonal flu vaccine\n\nWe give the flu vaccine every year from the start of September until the end of March. Patients aged 65 and over are offered a high-dose vaccine (Fluzone High-Dose), which gives a stronger immune response at that age. The flu vaccine can be given at the same appointment as a COVID-19 vaccine.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 32,
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "similarity_score": 0.40462643,
          "dense_rank": 5,
          "lexical_score": null,
          "lexical_rank": null,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Vaccinations\n## Travel vaccinations\n\nBook a travel vaccination appointment at least six weeks before you leave, because some vaccines need more than one dose or take time to become effective. Bring your travel dates and the list of countries you are visiting. We offer:\n\n- hepatitis A (Havrix): two doses six to twelve months apart, and one dose before travel protects you for the trip;\n- typhoid, either as an injection (Typhim Vi) given at least two weeks before travel, or as an oral vaccine (Vivotif) of four capsules taken on alternate days and finished at least one week before travel;\n- hepatitis B (Engerix-B): three doses over six months.\n\nWe do not offer the yellow fever vaccine, which can only be given at a registered yellow fever vaccination centre. We also do not offer rabies or Japanese encephalitis vaccines.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 32,
          "chunk_index": 4,
          "similarity_score": 0.38477063,
          "dense_rank": 6,
          "lexical_score": null,
          "lexical_rank": null,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Vaccinations\n## Self-pay vaccine prices\n\nIf your insurance does not cover a vaccine, these are the self-pay prices: flu vaccine $35, high-dose flu vaccine $70, Tdap $55, hepatitis A $85 per dose, ty",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 23,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.31443888,
          "dense_rank": 7,
          "lexical_score": null,
          "lexical_rank": null,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: Which health insurance plans do you accept?\nAnswer: We accept most major insurance providers, including Blue Cross Blue Shield, Aetna, Cigna, UnitedHealthcare, and Medicare. If you're unsure",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 22,
          "chunk_index": 0,
